{"term":"трань","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"tran'","category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"trans_slur","concept":"transgender_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":65,"recognition_pct_peak":65,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Offensive Russian slur for a transgender person, clipped from 'транс' (trans); used to mock or dehumanize trans individuals.","english_term":"tranny","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Functional parallel to English 'tranny'; uniformly offensive, not reclaimed; usage growing as trans visibility and anti-trans discourse both intensify in Russia."}
{"term":"извращенец","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"izvrashenets","category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"sexual_deviant","concept":"pervert","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":55,"technical":20,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A pervert or sexual deviant; a person with socially condemned or atypical sexual interests or behavior.","english_term":"pervert","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"The standard Russian word for 'pervert'; straddles colloquial and mildly formal register; applied broadly to any sexual nonconformist, not only those with clinical paraphilias."}
{"term":"петух","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"petukh","category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"prison_caste_slur","concept":"prison_sexual_caste","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"subculture","crude":90,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"In Russian prison slang (феня), the lowest-status caste: men who have been forcibly sexually degraded and are permanently stigmatized as receptive; widely used outside prison as an extreme insult implying total irreversible social degradation.","english_term":null,"english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Literal meaning 'rooster'; the феня caste-system concept has no direct English equivalent — American prison slang 'punk' is roughly analogous but lacks the same elaborate permanent-social-death framing and ritual enforcement; being labeled петух is considered irreversible within criminal subculture hierarchy."}
{"term":"дырка","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"dyrka","category":"insults","subcategory":"dehumanizing_objectification","concept":"sexual_objectification","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":75,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":92,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'hole'; used crudely for the vagina or anus, and pejoratively for a person — especially a woman or gay man — reduced to their sexual orifice, denying personhood.","english_term":"hole","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"As a body-part reference it is contextually crude; as a person-insult it fully dehumanizes by reducing the target to a mere receptacle; closer in register to 'she's just a hole' than to 'cunt,' which carries more active hostility."}
{"term":"опущенный","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"opushchennyy","category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"prison_caste_slur","concept":"prison_sexual_caste","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"subculture","crude":92,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'lowered/put down'; in Russian prison slang, a person who has been ritually or forcibly relegated to the петух caste through sexual humiliation; outside prison, an extreme insult for someone utterly and permanently socially degraded.","english_term":null,"english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The verb 'опустить' (to degrade someone into the петух caste) and this past-participle form name a concept pair with no English analogue: the idea of a permanent, ritually enacted sexual demotion that defines social status for life is specific to Russian/Soviet criminal subculture."}
{"term":"дегенерат","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"degenerat","category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"sexual_deviant","concept":"pervert","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":55,"technical":25,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A degenerate; a person considered morally or sexually depraved and beneath normal human behavioral standards.","english_term":"degenerate","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Loanword from German/Latin via early-20th-century scientific-racial discourse; retains pseudo-clinical flavor making it sound slightly more formal than 'извращенец'; widely deployed by Russian conservatives and Orthodox commentators as a catch-all condemnation of LGBTQ+ people."}
{"term":"содомит","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"sodomit","category":"religious_moral_status","subcategory":"sodomy_religious","concept":"sodomite","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"moral_religious","crude":60,"technical":35,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sodomite; a biblical and legal-historical term for a man who practices anal sex, especially with another man; carries inherent religious condemnation derived from Genesis 18–19.","english_term":"sodomite","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Direct cognate of English 'sodomite'; used in Russian Orthodox and conservative political discourse; carries heavier implied theological condemnation than the more neutral clinical term 'гомосексуалист'."}
{"term":"мужеложец","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"muzhelozhets","category":"religious_moral_status","subcategory":"sodomy_legal","concept":"sodomite","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"archaic","crude":50,"technical":40,"recognition_pct_current":70,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":1993,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'one who lies with men'; an archaic ecclesiastical-legal term for a man who engages in male-male anal intercourse; the specific term used in Soviet Criminal Code Article 121 (in force until 1993).","english_term":"sodomite","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Article 121 of the Soviet Criminal Code used this term; decriminalisation in 1993 generated its recognition peak in public discourse; now archaic except in Orthodox Church texts; heavier legalistic-ecclesiastical register than 'содомит'; the compound муже- (man) + лож- (lie/lay) is Church Slavonic in character."}
{"term":"ёб твою мать","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"yob tvoyu mat'","category":"insults","subcategory":"maternal_curse","concept":"motherfucker_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":97,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'fucked your mother'; one of the most powerful Russian mat curses, expressing extreme anger, contempt, or shock.","english_term":"motherfucker","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Structurally a past-tense declarative ('I fucked your mother') rather than the English nominal form 'motherfucker'; abbreviated in writing as ЁТМ; the maternal violation is a culturally salient axis of Russian obscenity that may carry greater symbolic weight than the English equivalent."}
{"term":"иди нахуй","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"idi nakhuy","category":"insults","subcategory":"dismissive_sexual_curse","concept":"fucker_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":90,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'go to the cock'; the canonical Russian directive meaning 'fuck off' or 'go fuck yourself.'","english_term":"fuck off","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Directional preposition 'на' + 'хуй' (cock/dick); parallel constructions: 'иди на хер,' 'иди в жопу'; among the most common dismissal phrases in Russian mat; deployed in anger, contempt, or exasperated dismissal."}
{"term":"нахуй","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"nakhuy","category":"insults","subcategory":"dismissive_expletive","concept":"fucker_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'to the cock'; standalone expletive meaning 'fuck off,' 'to hell with it,' 'no way,' or used as a general crude intensifier of negation and dismissal.","english_term":"fuck off","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Shorter standalone form of 'иди нахуй'; extremely versatile — intensifies refusals ('да нахуй!'), expresses disbelief, dismisses proposals, or punctuates contempt; one of the highest-frequency mat words in everyday spoken Russian."}
{"term":"пиздец","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"pizdets","category":"insults","subcategory":"catastrophic_expletive","concept":"shit_expletive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":92,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Derived from 'пизда' (cunt); used as a noun or interjection meaning 'it's all fucked,' 'total disaster,' 'we're doomed,' or 'the end'; the ultimate word for a complete and irredeemable catastrophe.","english_term":"clusterfuck","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Functions as a catastrophe noun ('это был пиздец' = 'it was a total disaster') and as a one-word doom verdict ('пиздец' = 'we're completely fucked'); closest English approximations are 'clusterfuck' or 'FUBAR,' though пиздец also functions as a standalone interjection of finality."}
{"term":"хуёво","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"khuyovo","category":"insults","subcategory":"negative_quality_expletive","concept":"shit_expletive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Derived from 'хуй' (cock/dick); a predicative adverb or short-form adjective meaning 'shittily,' 'terribly,' or 'it's bad/awful.'","english_term":"shitty","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Мне хуёво' = 'I feel like shit / I feel terrible'; 'всё хуёво' = 'everything sucks'; mirrors the grammatical slot of 'хорошо' (good/well) but is emphatically crude; one of several хуй-derived quality-descriptors covering negative states."}
{"term":"хуйня","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"khuyna","category":"insults","subcategory":"dismissive_noun_expletive","concept":"shit_expletive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":98,"recognition_pct_peak":98,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Derived from 'хуй' (cock/dick); a noun meaning 'bullshit,' 'nonsense,' 'crap,' or 'a worthless thing'; extremely versatile as a dismissive term for arguments, objects, or situations.","english_term":"bullshit","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"One of the most common mat nouns in everyday speech; grammatically feminine; dismisses arguments ('это полная хуйня' = 'this is total bullshit'), refers to broken or worthless objects, or expresses contempt for a situation; less specifically tied to deception than 'пиздёж'."}
{"term":"пиздёж","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"pizdyozh","category":"insults","subcategory":"lies_expletive","concept":"shit_expletive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":92,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Derived from 'пизда' (cunt); a noun specifically meaning 'blatant lies,' 'bullshitting,' or 'a pack of nonsense'; the verbal form 'пиздеть' means to lie or to talk obvious nonsense.","english_term":"bullshit","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"More semantically specific than 'хуйня' — пиздёж primarily connotes falsehood rather than general worthlessness; 'это пиздёж' = 'this is bullshit/lies'; the counterpart verb 'пиздеть' means specifically to bullshit or lie, distinguishing it functionally from other mat nouns."}
{"term":"мудак","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"mudak","category":"insults","subcategory":"contemptible_person","concept":"asshole_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Derived from archaic 'муда' (testicles); an asshole, jerk, or thoroughly contemptible person; one of the most common Russian insults for someone who is selfish, stupid, or unpleasant.","english_term":"asshole","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Among the most widely used mat insults in everyday Russian; gender-neutral in application despite the masculine-anatomical etymology; the root 'муда' survives only in derivatives such as мудак and мудила."}
{"term":"мудила","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"mudila","category":"insults","subcategory":"contemptible_person","concept":"asshole_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":82,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":82,"recognition_pct_peak":82,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"An emphatic variant of 'мудак'; a contemptible, stupid, or offensive person, with added contempt or colorfulness relative to the base form.","english_term":"asshole","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The suffix '-ила' adds intensity or pejorative emphasis; perceived as slightly more archaic or regional than мудак; the two forms are often interchangeable but мудила carries a heavier or more exasperated register."}
{"term":"ёбаный","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"yobany","category":"insults","subcategory":"intensifier_expletive","concept":"fucker_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Past passive participle of 'ёбать' (to fuck); used as an intensifying adjective meaning 'fucking,' as in 'ёбаный идиот' (fucking idiot), expressing disgust, exasperation, or emphasis.","english_term":"fucking","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Functions grammatically as an attributive adjective and applies freely to non-human targets ('ёбаная машина' = 'fucking car'); the exclamation 'ёбаный в рот!' is an extreme interjection of shock or irritation; one of the most productive mat modifiers in Russian."}
{"term":"блядь","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"blyad'","category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_whore","concept":"slut_shame","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":93,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"One of the five canonical Russian mat words; primary meaning 'whore' or 'slut'; secondary use as a general expletive equivalent to 'fuck!' or 'damn!' when deployed as a standalone interjection.","english_term":"whore","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Church Slavonic root meaning 'fornication/harlotry'; alongside хуй, пизда, ёбать, and пиздец forms the core of Russian mat; its standalone interjection function ('блядь!' expressing shock or pain) is as frequent as its person-insult function; both misogynistic target-insult and all-purpose expletive."}
{"term":"блядина","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"blyadina","category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_whore","concept":"slut_shame","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":92,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"An emphatic augmentative of 'блядь'; 'a total whore' — a more contemptuous form of the same insult, typically directed at a woman regarded as particularly promiscuous or contemptible.","english_term":"slut","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The suffix '-ина' creates an augmentative-pejorative; used primarily as a direct person-insult rather than a standalone expletive, distinguishing it from 'блядь' which freely serves both functions."}
{"term":"бляха","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"blyakha","category":"insults","subcategory":"minced_oath","concept":"slut_shame","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"euphemism","crude":25,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A minced oath substitute for 'блядь'; literally 'badge' or 'metal plate,' repurposed as a mild expletive for contexts where the full mat word is socially unacceptable.","english_term":"shoot","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The extended form 'бляха-муха' (literally 'badge-fly') is also common; phonetic proximity to 'блядь' carries the emotional resonance while avoiding the taboo; crude score is low because the word itself navigates around the transgression; widely used in media, at work, and around children."}
{"term":"ёбанутый","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"yobanuty","category":"insults","subcategory":"crazy_expletive","concept":"fucker_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":82,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Derived from 'ёбать' (to fuck); means 'crazy,' 'nuts,' or 'fucked in the head'; describes a person whose behavior is wildly irrational or beyond all reason.","english_term":"fucking crazy","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Not primarily a sexual insult despite its etymology; functions semantically like 'batshit crazy' or 'fucking nuts'; can be used with affectionate exasperation ('ты ёбанутый?' = 'are you crazy?') as well as genuine contempt; cf. ёбаный, which acts as an intensifier adjective rather than a descriptor of mental state."}
{"term":"шлюха","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"shlyukha","category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_shame","concept":"slut_shame","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Slut or whore; one of the most common Russian insults for a woman regarded as sexually promiscuous; also used as a general-purpose strong insult.","english_term":"slut","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Slightly less crude in register than 'блядь' (the canonical mat word for the same concept) but unambiguously offensive; derivation possibly from German 'Schlucht' or a Slavic root meaning to drag/trail; the standard non-mat equivalent of 'блядь' in the slut-shame register; the two words are largely interchangeable in practice."}
{"term":"потаскуха","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"potaskukha","category":"insults","subcategory":"promiscuous_woman_slur","concept":"promiscuous_woman_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"dated_slang","crude":65,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":78,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A dated Russian slur for a sexually promiscuous woman; 'tramp,' 'tart,' or 'trollop'; connotes a woman who chases after men or is sexually available, with an archaic flavor relative to 'шлюха'.","english_term":"trollop","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"From the verb 'тащить' (to drag/pull); the image is of a woman trailing after men; less vulgar than 'шлюха' and more archaic; more common in literature and older speech; recognition has declined among speakers under 35."}
{"term":"сука","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"suka","category":"insults","subcategory":"bitch_insult","concept":"bitch_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":82,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'female dog'; used as a general-purpose insult for a contemptible, unpleasant, or treacherous person, especially a woman; also carries the specific meaning of 'traitor' or 'snitch' in prison and criminal slang.","english_term":"bitch","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"The criminal-subculture secondary meaning (сука = informer/traitor) is an additional semantic layer absent from English 'bitch'; in everyday use closely parallels English 'bitch' in full range — woman insult, person-insult, intensifier, and occasionally a term of address between friends."}
